// title: ⚡ Lightning Round: Names With Nothing Behind Them
// date: 2026-11-12
// product: Sentinel
// tables: W3CIISLog
// purpose: From the article: KQL Detection of the Week: Two Things Called SharePoint
// source: https://devsecopsdadattack.com/2026-11-12-KQL-Detection-of-the-Week-Two-Things-Called-SharePoint/
// kind: article
// author: DevSecOpsDad · DevSecOpsDad (detection engineering briefs, KQL)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
W3CIISLog
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(7d)
| where csUriStem startswith "/certsrv/" and csMethod == "POST"
// Web enrollment is mostly for people. A machine account (DC01$)
// submitting a request here is consistent with ESC8 relay, and
// worth a look. It isn't proof: some legitimate automation enrolls
// through web enrollment too.
| where csUserName endswith "$"
| summarize Requests = count(), Pages = make_set(csUriStem, 5)
    by Computer, csUserName, cIP, bin(TimeGenerated, 5m)
